@* Plan N13 (pass 28b): a Starshell attempt at night (E1.92). The page gives the firing side's units that may try, already read for the view (ruling
   R23.1); the planner decides the Usage dr, the LOS and NVR for a shot at a target, and the Random Direction. The own-hex method needs no target. *@
<h4>Starshells</h4>
<RuleHelp Id="starshell-help" Summary="A Good Order leader, MMC, or CE AFV fires a Starshell after a successful Usage dr (4 or less for a leader, 2 or less otherwise), once per hex this phase; it Illuminates until the end of the CCPh, and firing it is not firing (E1.92, E1.923).">
    A Good Order leader, CE AFV, or MMC fires a Starshell after a Usage dr of 4 or less (a leader) or 2 or less, one attempt per hex this phase:
    in its own hex, then one hex in a Random Direction; at a Gunflash or Known enemy unit in its LOS within six hexes, then a Random Direction DR
    with the Extent of Error halved; or in a hex exactly three hexes away, then a Random Direction DR. It Illuminates three hexes around it until
    the end of the CCPh; firing it is not firing (E1.92, E1.923).
</RuleHelp>
<div class="toolbar">
    <label>Fired by
        <select id="starshell-unit" value="@Unit" @onchange="@(args => OnUnit.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">choose</option>
            @foreach (var id in Firers)
            {
                <option value="@id">@Say(id)</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    <label>method
        <select id="starshell-method" value="@Method" @onchange="@(args => OnMethod.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? OwnHex))">
            <option value="@OwnHex">its own hex</option>
            <option value="at-target">at a Gunflash or Known enemy unit within six hexes</option>
            <option value="three-hexes">a hex exactly three hexes away</option>
        </select>
    </label>
    <label>at <input id="starshell-at" value="@At" disabled="@(Method == OwnHex)" @onchange="@(args => OnAt.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))" size="12" /></label>
    <button id="propose-starshell" disabled="@(!Firers.Contains(Unit) || (Method != OwnHex && At.Trim().Length == 0))" aria-describedby="propose-starshell-ready" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync())">Propose: fire a Starshell</button>
    @if (!Firers.Contains(Unit) || (Method != OwnHex && At.Trim().Length == 0))
    {
        <span id="propose-starshell-ready" class="toolbar-note">Choose the firer, and the Location unless it fires into its own hex.</span>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The page's words for the view (pass 31c, design D11): a unit's name for its id, a Location in words.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "Say")]
    public Func<string, string>? Words { get; set; }

    private string Say(string? text) => text is null ? string.Empty : Words?.Invoke(text) ?? text;

    /// <summary>The method that fires in the firer's own hex and needs no target.</summary>
    public const string OwnHex = "own-hex";

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Firers { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Unit { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public string Method { get; set; } = OwnHex;

    [Parameter]
    public string At { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnUnit { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnMethod { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnAt { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnPropose { get; set; }
}
